# Dynamic Category System

## Adding a New Category

Only edit `src/shared/config/categories.ts` — nothing else:

```typescript
export const MOCK_CATEGORIES: CategoryConfig[] = [
  { id: '1', title: { TH: 'TADA MERCH',          EN: 'TADA MERCH' },          dataSource: 'products' },
  { id: '2', title: { TH: 'NADAO OFFICIAL GOODS', EN: 'NADAO OFFICIAL GOODS' }, dataSource: 'official-goods' },
  { id: '3', title: { TH: 'BUS COLLECTION',       EN: 'BUS COLLECTION' },       dataSource: 'products' },
  // ← add here
];
```

After adding, the category will automatically appear:
- **Home page** — as a new `<CategorySection>` (via `src/modules/home/components/CategorySection.tsx`)
- **Category page** — routed at `/category/[id]` (via `src/app/category/[id]/page.tsx`)

## Data Sources

| `dataSource` | Fetches from |
|---|---|
| `'products'` | `useProductList` hook |
| `'official-goods'` | `useOfficialGoods` hook |

To add a new data source type, update `DataSource` in `categories.ts` and add a branch in `src/modules/category/hooks/useCategoryItems.ts`.

## Rules

- **Never** hardcode category IDs or titles in components
- **Never** use `if (categoryId === '1')` — read from `getCategoryById(id)` instead
- Category titles are defined in config, NOT in `translations.ts`
- The home page uses `MOCK_CATEGORIES.map(...)` — order in the array = display order on home
